{%- comment -%}
  Deliberately repeat real merchandising renders to model a larger store with
  this small demo catalog. Captures execute on Shopify; their output is counted,
  not emitted. Keep this outside dynamic fragments and cart sections so an edge hit
  can reuse the completed page. Never derive this workload from cart/customer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.settings.enabled -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign source_collection = section.settings.collection | default: collections.all
    assign source_products = source_collection.products
    assign catalog_size = source_products.size | at_most: 48
    assign passes = section.settings.passes | default: 16 | at_least: 1 | at_most: 32
    assign slots = section.settings.slots | default: 48 | at_least: 8 | at_most: 48
    assign integrations = section.settings.integrations | default: 1 | at_least: 0 | at_most: 2
    if integrations > 0
      assign max_passes = 1536 | divided_by: slots | divided_by: integrations
      assign passes = passes | at_most: max_passes
    endif
    assign card_count = 0
    assign variant_checks = 0
    assign rendered_characters = 0
  -%}
  {%- if catalog_size > 0 -%}
    {%- for pass in (1..passes) -%}
      {%- for slot in (1..slots) -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign product_index = slot | minus: 1 | modulo: catalog_size
          assign candidate = source_products[product_index]
          assign variants = candidate.variants | sort: 'price' | slice: 0, 24
          assign variant_checks = variant_checks | plus: variants.size
          assign card_count = card_count | plus: 1
        -%}
        {%- capture card -%}
          {%- render 'edgemesh-merchandise-card', product: candidate, variants: variants -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if integrations > 0 -%}
          {%- for integration in (1..integrations) -%}
            {%- capture integration_payload -%}
              {%- render 'edgemesh-merchandise-integrations', product: candidate, variants: variants, catalog: source_products -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- assign rendered_characters = rendered_characters | plus: integration_payload.size -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- assign rendered_characters = rendered_characters | plus: card.size -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  <section
    class="em-liquid-section"
    aria-labelledby="em-liquid-title-{{ section.id }}"
    data-em-liquid-cards="{{ card_count }}"
    data-em-liquid-variants="{{ variant_checks }}"
    data-em-liquid-characters="{{ rendered_characters }}"
    data-em-liquid-integrations="{{ card_count | times: integrations }}"
  >
    <div class="em-container">
      <div class="em-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="em-eyebrow">{% render 'edgemesh-icon', name: 'server' %} HOW THIS DEMO WORKS</p>
          <h2 id="em-liquid-title-{{ section.id }}">A fast foundation.<br>A real store’s workload.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Shopify’s Horizon theme is a performant starting point. As a storefront grows, apps, merchandising rules, and richer product data add work. This demo models the extra Liquid processing those features can introduce.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="em-liquid-panel">
        <div class="em-liquid-simulation">
          <h3>Real Liquid work, simulated store complexity.</h3>
          {%- if catalog_size > 0 -%}
            <p>We reuse this small catalog to run a bounded set of product, variant, pricing, and metafield operations{% if integrations > 0 %}, plus app-style processing for reviews, related products, and structured data{% endif %}. The work runs on Shopify, without artificial delays or third-party apps. Repeated output stays on the server, so the comparison measures processing rather than an oversized page.</p>
          {%- else -%}
            <p>The simulation is ready, but the selected collection has no published products. Choose a populated collection in the theme editor to run the Liquid workload.</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="em-liquid-paths">
          <div>
            <h3>Fresh Liquid render</h3>
            <p>When Shopify executes the Liquid template, it assembles the theme and store data into a freshly rendered page. That HTML is returned from Shopify, the origin behind this demo. More Liquid work means more time before the page is ready.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Shopify HTML cache</h3>
            <p>Shopify can reuse previously rendered HTML to save that work. The origin response may contain an older snapshot that does not yet reflect a recent change. Shopify manages freshness and invalidation automatically; this Liquid theme has no direct controls for its cache lifetime or purging.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Edgemesh edge cache</h3>
            <p>An Edgemesh hit serves the page from our edge without a round trip to Shopify. This can be faster even than fetching Shopify-cached HTML. Edgemesh adds cache controls while dynamic fragments and Shopify’s Section Rendering API keep visitor-specific content, like the cart, current.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="em-liquid-hint">Use Server Vitals to compare these delivery paths. Open “How to read these numbers” to see more details. Disabling Edgemesh cache sends requests direct to Shopify who may return their own cached response. The fresh-render indicator is an estimate based on response time and the Liquid timestamp.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Liquid rendering workload",
  "settings": [
    {"type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enable server rendering workload", "default": true},
    {"type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "Source collection", "info": "Uses all products when empty. Samples the first 48 products."},
    {"type": "range", "id": "passes", "label": "Merchandising passes", "min": 1, "max": 32, "step": 1, "default": 16},
    {"type": "range", "id": "slots", "label": "Product slots per pass", "min": 8, "max": 48, "step": 8, "default": 48},
    {"type": "range", "id": "integrations", "label": "App-style integrations per slot", "min": 0, "max": 2, "step": 1, "default": 1},
    {"type": "paragraph", "content": "Demo only: repeats actual product-card and app-style Liquid. App renders are capped at 1,536 per page; passes are reduced when needed. Repeated output stays on the server. Shopify and Edgemesh can reuse cached HTML. Disable to measure a baseline."}
  ],
  "presets": [{"name": "Liquid rendering workload"}]
}
{% endschema %}
